<p>Yes. You can pay someone to apply for jobs for you. In 2026 the price depends on who does the work. AI application tools and basic application services usually cost tens to a few hundred dollars a month. Dedicated human assistants cost a few hundred to about a thousand dollars a month. Reverse recruiters, who also do outreach and coaching, publish roughly $1,500 to $5,000 a month. What you buy is the application work: finding roles that fit, preparing your materials, completing forms and keeping a record. Employers still decide who gets interviews and offers, so no honest provider can promise either.</p>
